$comment
IR spectrum: harmonic vibrational analysis with IR intensities.
Manual basis (Q-Chem 6.1.1):
  p.972  Sec 10.7.1 -- the vibman package computes frequencies plus infrared and
         Raman activities; analytic Hessian used when available, otherwise finite
         difference of gradients; CPSCF solved in segments automatically.
  p.973  DORAMAN (Raman intensities are OFF by default), VIBMAN_PRINT, CPSCF_NSEG.
  p.974  Example 10.28 -- standard OPT then FREQ two-segment job.
IR intensities are printed by DEFAULT: no keyword required.
  Output block: "INFRARED INTENSITIES (KM/MOL)" with "IR Intens:" and "TransDip".
Frequency scaling factors and spectral broadening have NO $rem switch in 6.1.1
  (FREQ_SCALE_FACTOR / FREQ_RANGE belong to $vibronic, i.e. vibronic electronic
  spectra, manual p.991-992) -> apply scaling and line broadening in post-processing.
$end

$molecule
0 1
C   0.0000000000   0.0000000000   0.0000000000
O   0.0000000000   0.0000000000   1.1300000000
$end

$rem
JOBTYPE                 OPT
METHOD                  cam-b3lyp
BASIS                   aug-cc-pVTZ
SCF_CONVERGENCE         8
MAX_SCF_CYCLES          200
GEOM_OPT_TOL_GRADIENT   30
GEOM_OPT_TOL_DISPLACEMENT 120
GEOM_OPT_TOL_ENERGY     100
MEM_TOTAL               40000
GUI                     2
$end

@@@

$molecule
read
$end

$rem
JOBTYPE                 FREQ
METHOD                  cam-b3lyp
BASIS                   aug-cc-pVTZ
SCF_GUESS               READ
CPSCF_NSEG              2
SCF_CONVERGENCE         8
MEM_TOTAL               40000
GUI                     2
$end
